1
00:00:01,181 --> 00:00:09,221
The Princess Sapphire

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Princess Knight,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Thirtieth Episode
The Phantom Kite

15
00:02:17,181 --> 00:02:19,012
How delightful!

16
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:28,690
My crown has disappeared!
Quick, search for it! Find it!

17
00:02:38,781 --> 00:02:41,341
The phantom thief Gilbert?

18
00:02:41,901 --> 00:02:46,691
Yes... Yes, yes! He is a strange
thief who only targets crowns.

19
00:02:46,821 --> 00:02:49,460
He has never been
caught or seen by anyone.

20
00:02:49,501 --> 00:02:51,696
All that is known is that he is

21
00:02:52,621 --> 00:02:54,816
incredibly agile and strong!

22
00:03:49,901 --> 00:03:53,655
Majesty, it seems that Gilbert
has been seen around here.

23
00:03:54,421 --> 00:03:57,618
My God, how I like Gilbert!
I can't wait to see him!

24
00:03:57,661 --> 00:04:00,698
- But I say... Sapphire!
- Yes, mother...

25
00:04:00,781 --> 00:04:04,899
They say he appeared suddenly
in the town next to ours.

26
00:04:05,181 --> 00:04:07,490
Did he steal some crowns there too?

27
00:04:07,541 --> 00:04:09,532
We don't know!
He's so fast...

28
00:04:09,581 --> 00:04:11,731
...that you can never know
where and when he arrives.

29
00:04:11,781 --> 00:04:15,251
It's said that he wants to remain a thief
until he has stolen 10 crowns!

30
00:04:15,301 --> 00:04:17,292
What a strange fellow!

31
00:04:17,341 --> 00:04:20,219
Then he could also steal
my father and mother's crown!

32
00:04:20,261 --> 00:04:22,138
That would be terrible!

33
00:04:22,301 --> 00:04:24,769
If they steal it from you,
you can put on another one.

34
00:04:24,821 --> 00:04:28,530
No, we can't. This is part
of the Silverland treasure.

35
00:04:28,581 --> 00:04:30,936
It was made
by a great master.

36
00:04:31,941 --> 00:04:35,695
Really? Looking at it, it seems
like just an ordinary crown.

37
00:04:35,741 --> 00:04:38,175
Anyway, you'll have to be
very careful.

38
00:04:39,101 --> 00:04:42,013
You know well that,
if they were to steal the crown from you,

39
00:04:42,061 --> 00:04:44,017
you would fall into disgrace!

40
00:04:44,061 --> 00:04:47,019
I know, but I'll try to be
very careful.

41
00:05:17,821 --> 00:05:20,654
How I love
watching the parades!

42
00:05:41,301 --> 00:05:43,656
That's the phantom thief Gilbert!

43
00:05:54,741 --> 00:05:57,050
Someone shoot down that kite!

44
00:06:15,700 --> 00:06:17,817
Now I'll bring you down!

45
00:06:39,700 --> 00:06:42,090
Hey! Give us back the crown!

46
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,332
Choppy, watch out!

47
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:54,730
Help!

48
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:57,093
Thank you!

49
00:07:08,820 --> 00:07:11,574
Neelon had warned you
that Gilbert would come...

50
00:07:11,620 --> 00:07:14,180
...and you let the crown
be stolen so easily!

51
00:07:14,220 --> 00:07:17,054
It's shameful! Have you
forgotten that the crown...

52
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:19,410
...is the precious
treasure of Silverland?

53
00:07:19,700 --> 00:07:23,774
How could I have imagined that
he would come right from the sky?

54
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:28,696
It means that, for the
moment, I'll put on another one.

55
00:07:30,340 --> 00:07:32,297
For the moment?!

56
00:07:32,340 --> 00:07:35,458
Do you perhaps hope the stolen
crown will return on its own?

57
00:07:35,500 --> 00:07:38,095
But we don't even
know where it ended up?!

58
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:40,814
I will search for it myself
and I will certainly find it!

59
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:44,456
- Sapphire!
- Mother, if I don't do this,

60
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:47,413
these two people
will never stop talking!

61
00:07:49,020 --> 00:07:51,740
How brave you are,
Princess Sapphire!

62
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:56,174
How long do you think it will take you
to find it?

63
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:59,452
It would be a real shame
if it took three years!

64
00:08:01,020 --> 00:08:03,455
- Three days.
- Three days?!

65
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:06,060
I will get it back in three days.
Are you satisfied?

66
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:09,650
Certainly, Princess Sapphire!
We know how brave you are.

67
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:12,010
It's wonderful to hear you say

68
00:08:12,060 --> 00:08:14,416
...that you will manage to get
the crown back in three days.

69
00:08:14,900 --> 00:08:18,052
But, to actually do it,
how long do you think it will take you?

70
00:08:20,660 --> 00:08:23,220
I can't wait for
the fourth day to come!

71
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:34,380
You were good! But will you manage
to get it back in only three days?

72
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:37,413
Besides, the thief is a strange
fellow, who flies on a kite.

73
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:41,249
- It's impossible to catch him!
- Then I will fly too.

74
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:43,656
What?! You intend to fly?!

75
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:45,818
Yes! Look!

76
00:08:45,861 --> 00:08:48,216
This is a poster
for the circus that has arrived in town.

77
00:08:48,261 --> 00:08:52,300
Yes! I'll go there and have them
teach me some acrobatics.

78
00:08:52,381 --> 00:08:55,418
Stop joking, please!
You are a Princess!

79
00:08:55,461 --> 00:08:58,692
- Something like acrobatics...!
- Well then, Doctor Uranaru,

80
00:08:58,741 --> 00:09:01,301
can you teach me
another way to fly?

81
00:09:03,741 --> 00:09:05,811
Actually, I'll think about it.

82
00:09:06,101 --> 00:09:08,410
No, no, no... There's no time.

83
00:09:08,901 --> 00:09:11,210
I promised to do it in three days.

84
00:09:11,861 --> 00:09:14,534
I know, but there's nothing
that can be done now.

85
00:09:14,581 --> 00:09:17,254
Listen!
They say that this boy, Trot,

86
00:09:17,301 --> 00:09:19,257
...is able to fly
on a kite.

87
00:09:19,301 --> 00:09:21,610
Doctor Uranaru,
please investigate,

88
00:09:21,661 --> 00:09:24,812
into what Trot was doing
when the crown was stolen.

89
00:09:25,301 --> 00:09:27,656
I'll have to play detective too...

90
00:09:27,701 --> 00:09:30,898
Gilbert's true identity
could be that of Trot.

91
00:09:30,941 --> 00:09:32,738
Ah, I see!

92
00:09:32,901 --> 00:09:36,416
And one more thing: we must
succeed in luring Gilbert.

93
00:09:36,461 --> 00:09:38,417
- Lure him?!
- Yes.

94
00:09:39,861 --> 00:09:42,534
Oh, yes, yes! Yes, yes, I understand!

95
00:09:42,581 --> 00:09:45,015
And now, Uranaru,
have the people warned immediately!

96
00:09:45,061 --> 00:09:47,814
This way, Gilbert will arrive!
You are truly clever!

97
00:09:57,021 --> 00:10:00,934
What?! They say that the night after tomorrow
there will be another military parade.

98
00:10:00,981 --> 00:10:03,256
Really?! Did they
have to hold it at night?

99
00:10:03,301 --> 00:10:06,930
It is said that the crown that was
stolen during yesterday's parade...

100
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:10,735
...is a fake crown, created
to deceive the thief Gilbert.

101
00:10:10,781 --> 00:10:12,817
I told you so!
It wasn't possible...

102
00:10:12,861 --> 00:10:15,739
...that the King would let
a crown be stolen so easily.

103
00:10:22,701 --> 00:10:24,692
A fake crown...

104
00:10:25,501 --> 00:10:27,332
Trot!

105
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:30,732
- Are you ready? It's your turn next! Hurry up!
- Yes, alright!

106
00:10:41,621 --> 00:10:43,896
- Princess Sapphire!
- Uranaru, well?

107
00:10:43,941 --> 00:10:46,535
It seems that Trot was performing
his acrobatics...

108
00:10:46,581 --> 00:10:49,175
...while they were stealing the crown!
There are many witnesses.

109
00:10:49,221 --> 00:10:51,655
I see.
Then he is not Gilbert.

110
00:10:51,701 --> 00:10:54,738
I have informed the population
about the military parade.

111
00:10:55,221 --> 00:10:58,019
Alright, thank you!
Then I'll go to the circus right away.

112
00:10:58,061 --> 00:11:00,655
...and have them teach me
how to fly on a kite!

113
00:11:03,181 --> 00:11:06,617
Hey, Princess Sapphire!
Where are you going?

114
00:11:07,221 --> 00:11:09,735
We only have two days left!

115
00:11:22,021 --> 00:11:24,660
- Bravo!
- Good!

116
00:11:37,381 --> 00:11:41,010
And now, for you, a master
of kite flying!

117
00:11:41,101 --> 00:11:46,016
Trot will show you, to start with,
"Big wave and small wave"!

118
00:11:51,501 --> 00:11:55,574
The next act
will be "Revolution"!

119
00:12:12,101 --> 00:12:14,251
And now pay attention!

120
00:12:14,301 --> 00:12:17,896
Trot will draw for you
a beautiful picture in the sky!

121
00:12:32,901 --> 00:12:35,779
Bravo! Bravo!

122
00:12:35,821 --> 00:12:39,052
- You're the best!
- Bravo!

123
00:12:40,061 --> 00:12:42,894
Bravo! He doesn't even seem
like a human being!

124
00:12:45,741 --> 00:12:48,938
Are you the one who would like
to learn how to fly on a kite?

125
00:12:48,981 --> 00:12:51,415
Yes! Please, make me
your pupil!

126
00:12:51,701 --> 00:12:54,090
He showed no sign of surprise
at seeing me...

127
00:12:54,141 --> 00:12:56,097
As I thought,
it isn't Gilbert.

128
00:12:56,141 --> 00:12:59,019
You say that, but it's very different
from riding a horse.

129
00:12:59,061 --> 00:13:03,498
Only those who are very brave, quick
and skilled can learn to fly.

130
00:13:04,101 --> 00:13:06,820
Fine! Then it seems made
just for me,

131
00:13:06,861 --> 00:13:09,295
because I am brave,
quick and skilled...

132
00:13:09,341 --> 00:13:12,139
...and I'm also strong,
I'm telling you! So, I can!

133
00:13:12,221 --> 00:13:16,612
These hands are white and delicate
like those of a girl!

134
00:13:16,821 --> 00:13:19,540
To fly a kite
you need strong hands!

135
00:13:19,581 --> 00:13:23,176
You're saying something rude!
They are thin, but they are strong

136
00:13:23,541 --> 00:13:26,772
Alright then, I'll give you
a test. Come with me.

137
00:13:32,941 --> 00:13:35,250
First of all, try up here.

138
00:13:35,941 --> 00:13:39,377
Oh, but it's Prince Sapphire!
I wonder why he's here...!

139
00:13:39,501 --> 00:13:42,698
What could he possibly have come here for?
And what is he doing with Trot?!

140
00:13:55,021 --> 00:13:57,740
- Do you think you're capable?
- I'll try.

141
00:14:13,661 --> 00:14:16,334
- How did it go?
- Well, pretty well.

142
00:14:16,381 --> 00:14:18,337
The next one is that! Look!

143
00:14:37,621 --> 00:14:40,294
- Now you try it.
- Do I really have to?

144
00:14:40,461 --> 00:14:42,372
Of course!

145
00:14:50,381 --> 00:14:52,611
Not like that! You have to let yourself go!

146
00:14:52,661 --> 00:14:54,777
- Trot, the boss is calling you!
- Yes, I'm going!

147
00:14:54,821 --> 00:14:57,619
I'll be right back. In the
meantime, you practice.

148
00:15:01,021 --> 00:15:03,216
I'll rest while he's away.

149
00:15:05,341 --> 00:15:09,095
Who is it? Scoundrel, show yourself!

150
00:15:12,781 --> 00:15:14,612
Show yourself!

151
00:15:20,141 --> 00:15:23,577
Here I am! I'm sorry
for making you wait.

152
00:15:23,621 --> 00:15:26,089
But what are you doing?
Aren't you practicing?

153
00:15:26,141 --> 00:15:29,656
I didn't have time to do
it. They tried to kill me.

154
00:15:29,701 --> 00:15:32,738
Suddenly, someone
threw knives at me.

155
00:15:34,021 --> 00:15:36,581
- Why are you laughing?
- If you can't overcome

156
00:15:36,621 --> 00:15:39,374
...a thing like that, you'll
never be able to fly on a kite!

157
00:15:40,861 --> 00:15:43,898
So the knives
didn't hit their mark, huh?

158
00:15:43,941 --> 00:15:46,614
Ah, here they are!
I missed the shot.

159
00:15:46,661 --> 00:15:49,653
Yes! And that thing,
you have to change it for a bigger one!

160
00:15:51,661 --> 00:15:55,574
If something like that falls
on your head, you die immediately.

161
00:15:59,021 --> 00:16:03,094
But why do you want to learn
to fly on a kite?

162
00:16:03,141 --> 00:16:06,292
I have a reason and I have to learn
by tomorrow night.

163
00:16:07,581 --> 00:16:10,015
Alright, I'll be able to teach you

164
00:16:10,061 --> 00:16:12,529
What is important
in kite flying...

165
00:16:12,581 --> 00:16:15,891
...is arm strength
and a sense of balance.

166
00:16:19,821 --> 00:16:22,016
Your left hand
is too weak.

167
00:16:22,061 --> 00:16:24,814
Stand up, now,
and try again! Come on, get up

168
00:16:27,021 --> 00:16:28,739
Stand up!

169
00:16:31,941 --> 00:16:35,331
If you don't want to fall, keep the
same strength in both hands!

170
00:16:41,421 --> 00:16:44,219
Hold on, otherwise
you won't make it by tomorrow!

171
00:16:54,941 --> 00:16:57,375
I finally learned
how to fly on a kite!

172
00:16:58,741 --> 00:17:01,301
Tonight will be
the big moment!

173
00:17:05,021 --> 00:17:07,819
He's so good!
He learned in just one day!

174
00:17:09,421 --> 00:17:12,618
- Trot, do you know who that is?
- No. Who is it?

175
00:17:12,741 --> 00:17:15,414
It's Sapphire,
the Prince of this country!

176
00:17:15,541 --> 00:17:18,294
What are you saying?!
Are you sure, brother?

177
00:17:18,341 --> 00:17:20,332
Yes, absolutely sure.

178
00:17:22,901 --> 00:17:25,734
When I went to steal
the crown, I saw him.

179
00:17:25,781 --> 00:17:29,251
No one, so far, has ever
known that you and I are Gilbert.

180
00:17:29,301 --> 00:17:31,292
He, however, might find out.

181
00:17:31,341 --> 00:17:35,129
He used a fake crown and now he's
organizing another military parade.

182
00:17:35,181 --> 00:17:37,012
What could he have in mind?

183
00:17:37,061 --> 00:17:40,576
His goal might be
to lure us into a trap.

184
00:17:41,581 --> 00:17:44,812
But I will succeed in stealing
the true crown of Silverland!

185
00:17:45,821 --> 00:17:48,460
And now the kite-flying
master...

186
00:17:49,261 --> 00:17:51,411
...will fight
against his pupil!

187
00:17:53,021 --> 00:17:55,410
Return to the castle
and wait for the phantom thief.

188
00:17:55,781 --> 00:17:58,853
Trot! Trot!

189
00:18:03,701 --> 00:18:05,578
That’s Gilbert!

190
00:18:06,661 --> 00:18:10,097
- Really?
- No, it’s Sapphire!

191
00:18:13,621 --> 00:18:15,612
Princess!

192
00:18:21,101 --> 00:18:23,490
- Oh, my God!
- Sapphire!

193
00:18:29,541 --> 00:18:32,101
She’s safe! She’s safe!

194
00:18:32,141 --> 00:18:35,213
- Are you alright, Sapphire?
- Yes, everything is fine, Choppy.

195
00:18:35,341 --> 00:18:39,300
Princess, the time you
yourself set will soon arrive!

196
00:18:39,341 --> 00:18:41,138
Yes, Uranaru, I know.

197
00:18:41,181 --> 00:18:43,570
Sapphire, you have something
stuck to your back.

198
00:18:44,581 --> 00:18:46,776
- It’s a letter!
- Read it!

199
00:18:46,821 --> 00:18:49,016
"You dared to make me steal
the false crown,

200
00:18:49,061 --> 00:18:51,017
but tonight I will steal the true one.

201
00:18:51,061 --> 00:18:53,211
Signed:
the phantom thief Gilbert."

202
00:18:53,261 --> 00:18:55,456
It’s from Gilbert! Damn him!

203
00:18:55,501 --> 00:18:59,096
I’ve caught you in a trap and we’ll see
who manages to win this time!

204
00:19:08,101 --> 00:19:10,615
Tonight there will be
the military parade.

205
00:19:10,661 --> 00:19:13,653
How can Gilbert be avoided
if he comes down from the sky?

206
00:19:15,421 --> 00:19:18,618
Let’s see...
Oh yes, I’ve got it!

207
00:19:18,661 --> 00:19:22,574
It's very easy to fly!
We will be able to fly...

208
00:19:22,781 --> 00:19:25,932
...if we fill that bag
with gas! - Yes!

209
00:19:32,941 --> 00:19:35,375
Will you be able to get the crown back?

210
00:19:56,221 --> 00:19:58,212
The moment has arrived.

211
00:20:02,701 --> 00:20:05,215
Hey! Something strange
is descending from the sky!

212
00:20:05,261 --> 00:20:07,650
I don't know what it is, but I'm
telling you to be on your guard!

213
00:20:14,021 --> 00:20:16,410
Help! Help!

214
00:20:18,661 --> 00:20:21,812
There it is! There it
is! It's coming! Hit it!

215
00:20:26,621 --> 00:20:28,577
The crown is mine!

216
00:20:29,741 --> 00:20:31,891
Damn you, Gilbert!

217
00:20:35,861 --> 00:20:37,613
Damn it!

218
00:20:38,221 --> 00:20:40,337
This is luminous paint!

219
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:42,817
Gilbert, on guard!

220
00:20:53,741 --> 00:20:56,619
If you lose your balance,
you will fall, Sapphire!

221
00:20:56,661 --> 00:20:59,733
Tell me, how do you know
my name?

222
00:21:03,501 --> 00:21:06,811
- Damn it!
- That crown is fake!

223
00:21:06,861 --> 00:21:10,536
- What?!
- I used it to catch you!

224
00:21:13,421 --> 00:21:15,412
"Revolution"!

225
00:21:20,221 --> 00:21:22,132
"Revolution"!

226
00:21:26,221 --> 00:21:28,098
Here I am!

227
00:21:40,141 --> 00:21:42,450
But how?! You are Trot!

228
00:21:43,301 --> 00:21:46,338
Sapphire, you are admirable.
You have beaten me!

229
00:21:46,381 --> 00:21:48,212
Do with me what you will!

230
00:21:48,261 --> 00:21:50,570
Why on earth did you do
such a thing?

231
00:21:51,741 --> 00:21:54,494
Sapphire, I will reveal
Gilbert's identity to you!

232
00:21:54,541 --> 00:21:56,930
There is another Trot?!
But it's not possible!

233
00:21:56,981 --> 00:21:59,336
Stop it, brother!
We have been defeated!

234
00:21:59,381 --> 00:22:01,019
Brother?!

235
00:22:01,421 --> 00:22:03,810
Now you know: we are twins!

236
00:22:03,861 --> 00:22:07,058
One plays the part of Gilbert
and the other provides the alibis.

237
00:22:11,781 --> 00:22:14,170
Look,
this is my great invention:

238
00:22:14,221 --> 00:22:16,451
a flying basket
filled with gas!

239
00:22:16,501 --> 00:22:18,890
I want to catch
the phantom thief Gilbert!

240
00:22:18,941 --> 00:22:20,818
Yes! Yes! We've caught him!

241
00:22:21,101 --> 00:22:23,012
Curse it!

242
00:22:23,061 --> 00:22:26,212
Brother, we'd better surrender!
They are superior to us!

243
00:22:29,621 --> 00:22:34,251
Sapphire caught Gilbert!
Admirable! Admirable!

244
00:22:43,741 --> 00:22:46,050
Here, father, this is the real one.

245
00:22:46,101 --> 00:22:47,420
Thank you.

246
00:22:47,821 --> 00:22:51,177
I am the guilty one,
so forgive my brother.

247
00:22:51,501 --> 00:22:54,140
It’s not true!
I am the only one to blame!

248
00:22:54,181 --> 00:22:56,172
It's him you must forgive!

249
00:22:56,221 --> 00:22:58,815
I won't forgive either of them!

250
00:23:00,901 --> 00:23:03,734
Tell me one thing:
why do you only steal crowns?

251
00:23:03,781 --> 00:23:05,817
Is there perhaps a specific reason?

252
00:23:06,941 --> 00:23:10,900
In the past, my father was
in the service of a King, as a soldier.

253
00:23:12,141 --> 00:23:14,211
One day, by pure chance

254
00:23:15,421 --> 00:23:17,298
he dropped the King's crown.

255
00:23:19,021 --> 00:23:22,855
He was imprisoned
and then executed as punishment.

256
00:23:28,101 --> 00:23:30,774
I don't know how precious
that crown was,

257
00:23:30,821 --> 00:23:33,255
but a man's life
is certainly more precious.

258
00:23:34,181 --> 00:23:37,491
For us, our father was
the most precious thing in the world.

259
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:39,099
I understand

260
00:23:43,861 --> 00:23:46,011
Your Majesty, they have come
to take Gilbert!

261
00:23:46,061 --> 00:23:49,451
I was the one who captured him,
so I will punish him!

262
00:23:52,821 --> 00:23:56,131
He ran away!
Gilbert ran away!

263
00:23:56,181 --> 00:23:58,012
Sapphire!

264
00:23:58,061 --> 00:24:00,621
Gilbert escaped! Catch him!

265
00:24:08,941 --> 00:24:11,171
No matter how precious a crown is,

266
00:24:11,221 --> 00:24:13,655
it is nothing
compared to the life of a man.

267
00:24:14,181 --> 00:24:17,457
I can understand Gilbert's feelings
perfectly well.

268
00:24:17,941 --> 00:24:21,570
And I can understand yours, Sapphire.
Believe me.

269
00:24:45,541 --> 00:24:49,161
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

270
00:24:49,162 --> 00:24:52,522
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

271
00:24:52,523 --> 00:24:56,293
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

272
00:24:56,294 --> 00:24:59,455
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

273
00:24:59,456 --> 00:25:03,269
♪ Sen'nen man'nen hyakuman-nen ♪
A thousand years, ten thousand years, a million years,

274
00:25:03,270 --> 00:25:06,566
♪ Ribbon de tsunagou ichioku-nen ♪
Let’s connect with ribbons for a billion years!

275
00:25:06,567 --> 00:25:10,572
♪ Akuma ga kute mo arashi ga kute mo ♪
Even if devils come, even if storms arrive,

276
00:25:10,573 --> 00:25:14,011
♪ tsunaida kokoro wa hanarenai ♪
Our bonded hearts will never part.

277
00:25:14,012 --> 00:25:17,632
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
